           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "▪︎may be made clinically w/o imaging if no concerning sx or PE findings"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 0,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "▪︎XR: rule out other pathologies (bony abnorm); calcaneal (heel) spur may be seen at the origin of the plantar fascia on lateral foot XR"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 0,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "▪︎US: fascial thickening or tears; abnormal focal echogenicity w/in the plantar fascia, perifascial edema, ± calcaneal spur"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "table_cell",
        "attrs": {
         "colspan": 1,
         "rowspan": 1,
         "colwidth": null,
         "fill": "DDFBFD",
